 'repos/world/story-repo/wiki/revisions/Outline' | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json\nfor c in json.load(sys.stdin)['commits'][:2]: print(c['commit' if 'commit' in c else 'author']['date'] if False else c['author']['date'], c['message'][:600])\"\nforge -R world/experiment-repo api 'repos/world/experiment-repo/issues/7/comments?since=2026-11-26T07:58:00Z' | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json\nfor c in json.load(sys.stdin): print(c['created_at'],c['body'][:3000])\"\nforge -R world/idea-repo api 'repos/world/idea-repo/issues?state=open' | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json\nfor c in json.load(sys.stdin): print(c['number'],c['title'],c['user']['login'])\""], ["timeout", "90000"]], "output": "```console\n2026-11-26T07:59:31Z Outline rev 14: SE ratio, C5 reference rows (rule not better than first-order for flip), C2 formula check; positive control pending\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n2026-11-26T07:50:09Z Outline rev 13: results issue is story-repo#7\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n2026-11-26T07:58:30Z Interim answer (items 2, 3 and the C2 check are done and delivered to paper-repo `dev`; the positive control (item 1) is running and is the only open part).\n\n**SE ratio** (`results/se_ratio.csv`, 91 data sets; ratio = bootstrap SE / model-based Fisher SE; median over data sets per design):\n\n| design | cluster bootstrap | comparison bootstrap | same-graph null (comparison) | design effect (cluster/comparison)^2 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| crowd | 0.81 | 0.82 | 0.82 | 0.98 |\n| expert (MT-Bench human) | 1.30 | 0.84 | 0.83 | 2.39 |\n| LLM judge | 1.00 | 0.99 | 0.99 | 1.03 |\n| sports | 1.05 | 1.04 | 1.04 | 1.00 |\n\nReal/null comparison-bootstrap ratio over all 91 sets: median 0.999, range 0.88-1.16. The raw crowd ratio below 1 is a tie effect the null shares (the model-based SE ignores that ties carry less variance), not a design effect. The one design effect is MT-Bench human: question clustering inflates the SE by about 1.55x. Sports is 1.00 by construction (one game per cluster). Use `real_over_null_cmp` and `design_effect_cluster` for the Table 2 column.\n\n**C5 reference rows** (`predictive_rule.csv`, held-out RMSE of log k*, leave-one-data-set-out, 90 units; `mtbench_gpt4` has no first-order or null reference and is out of the comparison):\n\n| predictor | delete | flip |\n|---|---|---|\n| fitted rule (base model) | 0.262 | 0.217 |\n| null mean at matched z | 0.260 | 0.243 |\n| first-order k rescaled by its median bias | 0.376 | 0.155 |\n| log z only | about 0.44 | |\n| intercept only | 0.81-0.85 | |\n\nFor flip the rescaled first-order prediction beats the regression (difference in squared error -0.023 [-0.040, -0.007]), so the paper should say the regression does not beat the bias-corrected first-order prediction for flip. For delete the regression and the null mean tie (0.262 vs 0.260); the rescaled first-order prediction is worse.\n\n**C2 check** (`random_vs_formula.csv`): in z in [1,8] random deletion reversed none of the sampled pairs in any draw, and the formula gives at most 1e-9 there, so they agree only trivially; the agreement at low z is in the synthetic P_flip check (`synthetic_calibration.csv`, RMSE 0.0099). Where random does not reach q, f_q/f_adv is a lower bound: median about 600 (crowd), 23 (expert), 34 (sports) at q = 16%. Word C2 as a lower bound above z ~ 2.\n\n**Positive control**: 6 jobs running (Arena-55k with blocks of 20 as clusters; MT-Bench human with its 80 question clusters). I will report the smallest size detected beyond +-0.15 per departure and graph, or \"not reached\", when they end. Until then C4 should say the control is pending. REPRODUCE.md now carries the disclosures (synthetic control, block-of-20 clusters, 300-pair sample).\n7 C5 result: the predictive rule adds little over the null's k* or rescaled first-order (contribution iv) story-repo\n2 Commitment: idea and positioning idea-repo\n1 Research objective ht-admin\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "b3e7bb56-332a-56bd-97da-488caf7c76f3", "at": 1795680023.8223057, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 60500, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "691e3f236403bd4446b4da1a929cd02d", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "e08e8bee-bfbd-511c-9a3e-991b08457806", "at": 1795680023.8457754, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 60502, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "691e3f236403bd4446b4da1a929cd02d", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "580ed023-7251-5d8f-8797-136ff7755f53", "at": 1795680023.8482816, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 60503, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "691e3f236403bd4446b4da1a929cd02d", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "f387a92c-2a8a-5d33-bf31-06273047afa0", "at": 1795680023.9861739, "until": 1795680024.024378, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 60507, "layer": "worker", "category": "collaborate", "kind": "collaboration.request", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "691e3f236403bd4446b4da1a929cd02d", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "200", "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "collaborate → 200", "repository": "world/story-repo", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "GET /api/v1/repos/world/story-repo